# MonteFiskal integration

Briefing: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atakancelik/MonteFiskal/main/docs/ai/context.md
Prompts: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atakancelik/MonteFiskal/main/docs/ai/prompts/README.md

## Rules for this task

- Ask the intake questions (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atakancelik/MonteFiskal/main/docs/ai/questions.md)
  before writing code. Never ask for a certificate, a key or a password; ask where the application reads them from.
- Do not invent codes, tax numbers or tax treatment. If a rule is not in the rule book or is not officially settled,
  say so and give the documented default.
- Use the test environment and the fake service only. Do not call production.
- Use the library for IKOF, signing, numbering and XML. Do not reimplement them.
- Finish with the prompt's verification and show its output.

## Mistakes to avoid

1. Computing the IKOF yourself instead of calling the library (BR-I1).
2. Floating-point money (BR-A5).
3. Treating a consumer card payment as non-cash (BR-K3).
4. Generating a new invoice number on retry (BR-O7).
5. Sending to production from a test (BR-T1).
6. Inventing `SoftCode` or `MaintainerCode` (BR-R7).
7. Storing the certificate in the repository or the web root (BR-S1).
8. Deleting or updating a fiscalized invoice instead of issuing a corrective (BR-C1).
9. Applying Croatian, Serbian or Albanian rules.
10. Skipping the initial cash deposit on a day with cash invoices (BR-D5).
